  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat oven to 425°F."
    },
    {
      "text": "Place flatbreads on a baking sheet pan; drizzle with oil, season with spices, and sprinkle with cheese. Place flatbreads in the oven (it doesn't have to be fully heated) and bake until crispy, 8-10 minutes."
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, wash, dry, trim, and small dice celery. Place in a medium bowl."
    },
    {
      "text": "Drain and rinse lentils. Add to the bowl with the celery along with mayo, dressing, and salt. Stir to combine the lentil salad."
    },
    {
      "text": "Wash, dry, and trim tomatoes. Slicing from the top down, cut tomatoes into wedges, being careful to not cut completely through to the bottom; sprinkle with salt."
    },
    {
      "text": "When the flatbreads are done, remove from oven and slice crosswise into 2-inch wide strips."
    },
    {
      "text": "Divide tomatoes between plates and stuff with lentil salad. Serve with cheesy breadsticks on the side and enjoy!"
    }
  ]
